<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n112392" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρούρ-ιον</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρώριον</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			<u>Inscr.Cret.</u>
			1 xvi 17
		</span></i>.<i><span class="en">
			15
		</span></i> (Lato, <span class="entity">ii B. C.</span>), τό,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fort, citadel,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				919
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12.93.17
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντὶ τοῦ πόλις εἶναι φρούριον
					κατέστη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					7.28
				</span></i>
			: esp. <i>hill-fort,</i> as distd. from a fortified town,
				<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				2.18
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				3.18
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				51
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				12.40
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				1.4.16
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βίον ὡς οἰκτρὸν ἐξαντλοῦσιν οἱ τὰ φ.
					τηροῦντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Men.
					74
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ φ. καὶ τὰ ὅρια τῆς Ἀττικῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					22.1028.22
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>prison,</i> of the body, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ax.</u>
				366a
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>garrison,</i> of a place, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				801
			</span></i> (where Sch. also expl. by <i>thing to be guarded
			against</i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φυλασσόμεσθα φρουρίοισι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Or.</u>
					760
				</span></i>
			 (troch.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλεως φ.,</span> of the
			Areopagites, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				949
			</span></i> (anap.).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
